WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.153 --> 00:00:01.233
- I remember in fourth grade,

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:03.497
everyone had to bring in a box of tissues.

00:00:03.497 --> 00:00:05.110
I have a strong memory of that.

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:06.736
I don't remember learning too much,

00:00:06.736 --> 00:00:09.587
but I remember I had to
bring in my box of tissues.

00:00:09.587 --> 00:00:11.353
(funk music)

00:00:12.483 --> 00:00:14.474
- [Voiceover] Explain photosynthesis.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.365
- (sighs) I know what this is,

00:00:20.365 --> 00:00:22.422
I think it's like when a flower...

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:23.035
(laughs)

00:00:23.035 --> 00:00:26.005
- This is when the sun is shining

00:00:26.005 --> 00:00:29.179
on flowers and things

00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:33.210
and there's rain and (laughing)
this is how things grow.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.043
- Plants receive light from the sun

00:00:35.043 --> 00:00:37.411
and they like, stay alive.

00:00:37.411 --> 00:00:40.057
- The plant takes in water and sunlight

00:00:40.057 --> 00:00:43.062
through the cell wall and
converts it to energy.

00:00:43.062 --> 00:00:43.649
(bell dings)

00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:45.646
- [Voiceover] What are the
three branches of government?

00:00:45.646 --> 00:00:47.259
- God, I should know this.

00:00:47.259 --> 00:00:48.664
I'm an adult. Dammit.

00:00:48.664 --> 00:00:53.099
- Judicial, legislative, Obama.

00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:54.608
- I've been watching a
lot of House of Cards

00:00:54.608 --> 00:00:55.666
but that's not helping.

00:00:55.666 --> 00:00:58.288
- There's the executive
branch, which is the president,

00:00:58.288 --> 00:01:00.901
the judicial branch, which
is the Supreme Court,

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:03.780
and then there is the legislative branch,

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.300
which is the Senate and Congress.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.261
(bell dings)

00:01:07.261 --> 00:01:09.127
- [Voiceover] The American
Civil War, when was it?

00:01:09.127 --> 00:01:11.507
- (laughing) I do not know.

00:01:11.507 --> 00:01:14.943
- Was that before World
War I and II or after?

00:01:14.943 --> 00:01:16.987
- I don't think it was that early.

00:01:16.987 --> 00:01:20.145
- 1960s? No, no, no.

00:01:20.145 --> 00:01:22.269
Maybe it was before.

00:01:22.269 --> 00:01:23.709
1930s?

00:01:23.709 --> 00:01:26.669
- Columbus sailed the ocean blue in 1492.

00:01:26.669 --> 00:01:28.550
He's a huge asshole, Columbus.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:32.730
- The American Civil War
was between 1861 and 1865.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:33.903
(bell dings)

00:01:33.903 --> 00:01:37.944
- [Voiceover] What is 23 divided
by four in mixed numerals?

00:01:37.944 --> 00:01:39.603
- So, that means...

00:01:39.603 --> 00:01:42.969
- This is like, how many vodka
sodas I can have in one night

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.945
divided by the number of
hours it probably takes

00:01:44.945 --> 00:01:46.186
for me to metabolize.

00:01:48.356 --> 00:01:51.022
(muttering)

00:01:51.022 --> 00:01:54.389
- I feel like I've completely
forgotten how to divide things

00:01:54.389 --> 00:01:57.641
but multiplication's still there, so...

00:01:57.641 --> 00:02:00.850
- Four, eight, 16, 20,

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.405
and then if it were 24,
it'd be five, obviously.

00:02:05.151 --> 00:02:07.625
Yeah. No. Six, it'd be six.

00:02:07.625 --> 00:02:09.749
- 20, wait, yeah.

00:02:09.749 --> 00:02:11.666
Right. What?

00:02:11.666 --> 00:02:12.605
Is that right?

00:02:12.605 --> 00:02:15.728
- Is this the mixed numerals?

00:02:15.728 --> 00:02:19.327
- It's four and 3/4, right?

00:02:19.327 --> 00:02:21.870
No, wait, that's not right.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.448
- Brunch is $23, divided by four people.

00:02:24.448 --> 00:02:27.327
- You finally stumped me
with this simple division

00:02:27.327 --> 00:02:29.985
that a fourth grader
would definitely know.

00:02:29.985 --> 00:02:33.753
- Yeah, it's like five
bucks, $5.10 each, I think.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.709
- That's the answer key.

00:02:35.709 --> 00:02:36.935
Boobless.

00:02:40.307 --> 00:02:42.467
- Also, just for like, kids watching,

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:44.591
college is way easier
than the fourth grade.

00:02:44.591 --> 00:02:46.030
Like, way easier.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.720
You like, talk about your
opinion and then you leave.

